<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Lay Trap</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Ranger (guild level 28)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>lay &lt;trap&gt;
</pre>
<p>Example:
</p>
<pre>lay trap
</pre>
<p>Sets a trap you carry, such as one made with <a cmd='#'>Help Fashion Weapon</a>, 
hidden on the ground where you stand. It costs endurance, more indoors 
and in cities than in the open. It can't be laid on water (it sinks), or 
where another trap is already hidden.
</p><p>How well it is hidden depends on your skill, dexterity and brain, the 
trap's quality, and the ground: deserts, forests, hills and snow hide a 
trap well, swamps, indoors and ice badly. You never step in your own 
trap.
</p><p>Anyone else who moves or looks around in the room may spring it, unless 
they spot it first; a monster just wandering in will too. A trapped 
victim can't move or do much more than look, talk and cast spells until 
the trap breaks, and if both of you have signed the Book of Blood, or the 
victim is a monster, struggling in it hurts. Attacking the victim breaks 
the trap, painfully. The trap breaks by itself after a few minutes, 
sooner for a poor one, caught or not.
</p><p>Others can look for hidden traps with search trap.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Fashion Weapon</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Search</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Ranger Skills</a>
</pre>




</div>